Magnetic field due to wire $A B$ and wire $E D$ cancel each other. So, magnetic field due to BC and ET will be

$$
\begin{aligned}
& B_1=\frac{\mu_0 I}{4 \pi(a / 2)} \cdot\left(\sin \frac{\pi}{2}+\sin 0^{\circ}\right) = \frac{\mu_0 I}{2 \pi a} \\
& B_2=\frac{\mu_0 I}{4 \pi(a / 2)} \cdot\left(\sin \frac{\pi}{2}+\sin 0^{\circ}\right) = \frac{\mu_0 I}{2 \pi a}
\end{aligned}
$$

So, $B_{\text {net }}=B_1+B_2=\frac{\mu_0 I}{\pi a}$

